            <div xml:id="d912">

                <pb facs="0819" n="647" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg647"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 124.55/8</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Belgium</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Whitlock</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-03-01T17:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 1, 1917, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>261. Department’s 256, February 26, 5 p.m., and your 44, February 26, 7 p.m.
                    Department wishes to avoid giving appearance that either Legation or commission
                    is withdrawing voluntarily from Belgium. Inasmuch as all former privileges to
                    members of relief commission have apparently been restored, you should not leave
                    until instructed further. Hoover wishes
                    members of commission to remain for the present but to depart with you in case
                    of your withdrawal.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
